A||||6||Gokart||Oil additive to raise compression??
Z||000000||Gokart||07-20-99||07:28 PM||||Is there an additive to help this problem with compression I'm having so I might sneak a few more miles on my borrowed time engine? I never believed much in additives, but if my engine is on it's way out I don't see the harm.
Z||000001||theogre||07-20-99||07:35 PM||||if the motor is this bad,,,, likely not much short of ripping it appart will help. JC whitless had something they claim helps,,,, you drop some pellets in the cylenders.... not sure I like that idea myself.
Z||000002||ezsurf||07-20-99||08:10 PM||||The only additive I know of that has been tested and proven to restore compression is a product called Engine Restore.  It comes in a silver can and is available at Auto Zone, Wal-Mart, and most auto parts stores.  Ogre is right though, this might buy you some time but the engine needs a rebuild.  But, if the funds aren't available, I'd go ahead and try it.  The only accurate way to tell if it made a difference though, is to do a compression check before and after.
Z||000003||lowCG||07-20-99||11:35 PM||||Ogre,you bring me back to a time when I tried the "engine overhaul pellets"from whitney in this Cortina GT,actually I made my little sister do it(pour them into the spark plug holes),took pictures,it was quite funny to us then anyways.I think the pellets worked for the first second or two,until they blew out of the engine!<br>I would put 20/50 Kendall along with a set of hotter spark plugs in and start hunting down a motor,and a mechanic.
Z||000004||Linx||07-21-99||12:18 AM||||It may not be rings...could be valves.  Squirt a shot of oil in the cylinder, and then check the compression.  If it doesnt change, then it's probably valves or head gasket.  And I'd rather change a gasket than replace rings.
Z||000005||PaUL||07-22-99||07:09 PM||||One sure way to find out is to remove the heads and see if there is a ridge on the top of the cylinder walls. If there is, the engine should be bored and new oversized pistons installed. 
Z||000006||Gokart||07-22-99||07:18 PM||||Won't bother with RESTORE for now! Thanks for your help. My loss in power was due to a loose wire! 
